# ==========================================================================
# CNSPK · Cloudflare Pages response headers  (task 16.1 · Requirements 2.1–2.3)
# ==========================================================================
# Cloudflare Pages parses this file and applies the rules to static asset
# responses. It is NOT served as an asset itself.
#
# STATUS TODAY: the live site at cloudnativesecurity.pk is still served by
# GitHub Pages (Cloudflare handles DNS only), and GitHub Pages ignores this
# file. So this file is an inert no-op in production right now — it starts
# sending real headers the moment the Cloudflare Pages project serves the
# domain. See DEPLOY.md for the ordered, zero-downtime cutover and for the
# free Cloudflare Transform Rule that can inject the same five headers on
# top of GitHub Pages today.
#
# NOTE: Pages Functions (functions/api/*) build their own responses; headers
# declared here are applied to static assets, so the /api/* handlers must set
# any headers they need in code.
#
# HOW THE ALLOWLIST BELOW WAS DERIVED (not guessed):
# It is the union of the `Content-Security-Policy` <meta> tags already shipped
# on every non-legacy page (index, about, join, events, sessions, sessions/view,
# members, team, speakers, projects, wins, labs, cfp, dispatch, brand,
# consultants, code-of-conduct, linktree) plus the origins those pages and
# their modules actually load:
#   cdn.tailwindcss.com          Tailwind Play CDN            (members, team, events, brand, sessions)
#   cdn.jsdelivr.net             DOMPurify 3.0.6              (members, team, sessions, join)
#   unpkg.com                    Leaflet 1.9.4 JS + CSS + its marker/shadow PNGs
#                                (leaflet.css references images/marker-icon.png
#                                 relative to unpkg.com, so unpkg must be in img-src)
#   fonts.googleapis.com         Google Fonts stylesheet      (@import in css/tokens.css)
#   fonts.gstatic.com            Google Fonts font files
#   *.basemaps.cartocdn.com      map tiles actually used by js/Map.js (Dark Matter, OSM data)
#   *.tile.openstreetmap.org     OpenStreetMap tile hosts — Leaflet's default layer and the
#                                documented fallback if the Carto layer is swapped out
#   docs.google.com              published Directory_CSV host + the Google Forms
#                                /formResponse POST target + the hidden form-sink frame
#   *.googleusercontent.com      where the published-to-web Sheets CSV redirects
#   sheets.googleapis.com        Sheets read path in js/members-source.js
#   api.github.com               GitHub intake/status reads
#   images.unsplash.com          current (placeholder) session/event imagery — task 14.4
#                                replaces these with labeled local placeholders; drop the
#                                origin from img-src once that lands
#   community.cncf.io            CNCF-hosted team photos (data/team.json)
#   avatars.githubusercontent.com  GitHub avatars
#   ui-avatars.com               speaker-avatar onerror fallback (SessionCard, SessionDetail)
#   www.youtube.com              session recording embeds (js/SessionDetail.js iframe)
#   'self'                       everything local, including the same-origin /api/* fetches
#
# DIRECTIVES DELIBERATELY LOOSENED, AND WHY (honest list):
#   1. script-src 'unsafe-inline'
#      Every page carries inline <script> blocks: the `tailwind.config = {...}`
#      block, the `<script type="module">` Navbar/Footer mount + scroll-reveal
#      IIFE, and JSON-LD. Nonces/hashes cannot be expressed in a static
#      `_headers` file (no per-request templating), so removing this would break
#      every page. Mitigation: no user-controlled string ever reaches a script
#      context, and all rendered data goes through js/lib/sanitize.js (DOMPurify).
#   2. style-src 'unsafe-inline'
#      Two hard reasons: (a) every page has a large page-scoped <style> block and
#      js/Navbar.js + js/Footer.js inject a <style> element at runtime;
#      (b) the Tailwind Play CDN writes its compiled CSS into an injected style
#      element. Also several components set inline style attributes.
#   3. img-src data:
#      Inline data: URIs are used for small inline SVG/graphics and the Leaflet
#      shadow fallback.
#   4. Wildcards are subdomain-only and never in script-src:
#      *.basemaps.cartocdn.com (a/b/c/d tile subdomains),
#      *.tile.openstreetmap.org, *.googleusercontent.com (Sheets CSV redirect
#      target, whose subdomain is not stable). No `*` host appears in script-src.
#   5. frame-src includes docs.google.com and www.youtube.com
#      js/MembershipForm.js POSTs to Google Forms through a hidden iframe sink
#      (Google Forms has no CORS for fetch), and session recordings embed YouTube.
#   6. form-action includes mailto: and docs.google.com
#      The membership form posts directly to Google Forms, and the intake forms
#      fall back to a labeled mailto: when an /api/* endpoint is unconfigured
#      (Requirement 19.3).
#
# NOT loosened: no 'unsafe-eval'. The Tailwind Play CDN runs fine without it —
# the pages already enforce these same meta policies in the browser today with
# no eval allowance, so script-src stays eval-free.
#
# TIGHTENED vs. the meta tags: frame-ancestors is 'none' here, not 'self'.
# `frame-ancestors` is ignored inside a <meta> CSP, so it only becomes real once
# it is sent as a header. Nothing on the site frames its own pages, so 'none' is
# safe and it pairs with X-Frame-Options: DENY for older agents.
#
# Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin — chosen because it is strict
# where it matters and breaks nothing. Cross-origin requests (Google Fonts,
# unpkg, tile hosts, the Google Forms POST) send only the origin, never the path,
# so a member's or session's URL never leaks to a third party; HTTPS→HTTP
# downgrades send nothing at all; and same-origin navigation keeps the full
# referrer, which the site's own relative links and the /api/* handlers rely on.
# `no-referrer` would be marginally stricter but would strip same-origin context
# for no real privacy gain here.
# ==========================================================================

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://cdn.tailwindcss.com https://cdn.jsdelivr.net https://unpkg.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com https://cdn.jsdelivr.net https://unpkg.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data: https://unpkg.com https://images.unsplash.com https://community.cncf.io https://avatars.githubusercontent.com https://ui-avatars.com https://*.basemaps.cartocdn.com https://*.tile.openstreetmap.org; connect-src 'self' https://api.github.com https://sheets.googleapis.com https://docs.google.com https://*.googleusercontent.com; frame-src 'self' https://docs.google.com https://www.youtube.com; form-action 'self' mailto: https://docs.google.com; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
